{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"READY TO CLOSE, pending one fresh plan review. All four children are closed: b00f, d8ef, b300, b5fe.\n\nEVERY MEASURED AC TARGET IS MET:\n    src/rebar/llm/config.py                    631   (AC: at or below 640; was 793)\n    src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py  511   (AC: at or below 560; was 794)\n    src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py              243   (AC: at least 100, under 800)\n    src/rebar/llm/plan_review/decide_ops.py    349   (AC: at least 100, under 800)\nPlus: seam guards exist for both relieved files with per-file bounds; the full plan-review step-registry membership test exists and runs in a SUBPROCESS; every 'uses:' in gates/plan-review.yaml is asserted to resolve; gen_env_registry is clean AND complete after b00f registered _llm_float; and every relocation landed with ZERO edits to existing tests beyond the two mandated headroom tightenings.\n\nWHY A FRESH REVIEW IS NEEDED, and it is a cost I chose knowingly: the signed attestation reads 'stale-head (UNSCOPED)'. It was signed BEFORE I set file_impact on this epic. Setting file_impact scopes FUTURE attestations; it does not retroactively scope one already signed. So the existing signature dies on every commit — which is precisely why I scoped the ticket mid-flight rather than leaving it. The next review will be scoped and will survive commits that do not touch its declared dependencies.\n\nDELIBERATELY SERIALISED: not launching that review yet, because d23e's round-3 review is in flight and d23e is the critical path. The one time two plan reviews overlapped in this session, a review reported findings against ticket text that had already been superseded. Cheap to avoid by waiting.\n\nWHAT THIS EPIC DID NOT DO, so the record is honest: it relieved the two files that were BLOCKING work and it did not drain the tier. plan_review/passes.py and _engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py both still sit at EXACTLY 800 with no ticket; attest.py is c6c9; signing.py is 798. And every cut here RELOCATED mass rather than dissolving an absorber — config.py's per-knob cost and decide's 213 lines are unchanged. The seam tests are the substitute ratchet for the per-function gate the operator declined."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785584535436294001,"uuid":"b5db7682-c058-43be-bcf3-79b59c42c3b3"}